I take the bicycle again.
I ride back to town.
I park my bicycle outside.
Then I go back into the shop.
I walk straight to the customer service desk.
A shop assistant is standing there.
"Good afternoon," I say politely to her.
"Good afternoon!"
"How can I help you?" she asks kindly.
I open my backpack.
I take out the yellow shirt.
"I bought this shirt here earlier," I explain.
"But unfortunately it is too small for me."
"I would like to exchange it."
The shop assistant smiles at me.
"That is of course no problem," she says.
"Do you have the receipt with you?"
"Yes, of course," I answer.
I place the shirt and the receipt on the counter.
